━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
[/CENTER]


[SIZE=4][COLOR=#e67e22]■[/COLOR] [B]Setup Guide[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#e67e22]Step 1 — Install[/COLOR][/SIZE]

Drop [ICODE]JExVote.jar[/ICODE] into your [ICODE]plugins/[/ICODE] folder and restart the server. JExVote generates its configuration files, an RSA keypair, and a Votifier token on first launch.

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#e67e22]Step 2 — Configure the Votifier server[/COLOR][/SIZE]

Open [ICODE]config.yml[/ICODE] and check the [ICODE]votifier[/ICODE] section:

[CODE=YAML]
votifier:
  host: ''          # Leave empty to bind all interfaces
  port: 8192        # The port vote sites connect to
  token: ''         # Auto-generated on first run — copy this to your vote site settings
[/CODE]

If your host requires a specific bind address, set [ICODE]host[/ICODE] accordingly. The [ICODE]token[/ICODE] is generated automatically — copy it from the config after the first start and paste it into your vote site's Votifier settings.

[B]Important:[/B] Make sure port [ICODE]8192[/ICODE] (or whatever you set) is open in your firewall / hosting panel. Vote sites need to reach this port directly.

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#e67e22]Step 3 — Add vote sites[/COLOR][/SIZE]

Edit [ICODE]sites.yml[/ICODE] to register each voting site:

[CODE=YAML]
sites:
  serverliste:
    display-name: "Serverliste.net"
    service-name: "Serverliste"        # Must match what the site sends
    vote-url: "https://serverliste.net/vote/12345"
    cooldown-minutes: 1440             # 24-hour rolling window
    points-per-vote: 1

  mcserverlist:
    display-name: "MC Server List"
    service-name: "MCServerList"
    vote-url: "https://minecraft-server-list.com/server/12345/vote/"
    daily-reset: "00:00"              # Fixed daily reset
    timezone: "Europe/Berlin"
    points-per-vote: 2
[/CODE]

[B]Cooldown modes[/B] — pick one per site:
[LIST]
[*][ICODE]cooldown-minutes[/ICODE] — Rolling window. The player can vote again X minutes after their last vote.
[*][ICODE]daily-reset[/ICODE] + [ICODE]timezone[/ICODE] — Fixed reset. Everyone can vote again at the specified time in the given timezone.
[/LIST]

The [ICODE]service-name[/ICODE] must exactly match the service identifier that the vote site sends in its Votifier payload. If you are unsure, use [ICODE]/jexvote fakevote <player> TestService[/ICODE] or check your server log for the incoming service name. Use [ICODE]/jexvote debug-services[/ICODE] to diagnose mismatches between configured and received service names.

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#e67e22]Step 4 — Configure rewards[/COLOR][/SIZE]

Open [ICODE]rewards.yml[/ICODE] to set up what players receive when they vote:

[CODE=YAML]
default-rewards:
  - type: command
    command: "give {player} diamond 1"
    as-console: true
  - type: sound
    sound: ENTITY_PLAYER_LEVELUP
    volume: 1.0
    pitch: 1.2
  - type: title
    title: "<green>Thank you!"
    subtitle: "<gray>Your vote has been counted."
    fade-in: 10
    stay: 40
    fade-out: 10
[/CODE]

Rewards are split into categories:

[LIST]
[*][B]default-rewards[/B] — Granted on every vote, regardless of which site the vote came from.
[*][B]streak-rewards[/B] — Bonus rewards at specific streak milestones (day 7, 14, 30, etc.).
[*][B]site-rewards[/B] — Extra rewards for voting on a specific site, keyed by site ID from [ICODE]sites.yml[/ICODE].
[*][B]vote-party-rewards[/B] — Granted to every contributor when a vote party completes (Premium).
[/LIST]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#e67e22]Step 5 — Verify[/COLOR][/SIZE]

Use [ICODE]/jexvote fakevote <yourname>[/ICODE] to trigger a test vote and confirm that rewards, broadcasts, and the GUI all work correctly. Check the console output — JExVote logs every vote it receives with the protocol version and service name.


[CENTER]
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
[/CENTER]


[SIZE=4][COLOR=#9b59b6]■[/COLOR] [B]Reward Types[/B][/SIZE]

All 14 reward types and their configuration keys:

[SPOILER="Full Reward Reference"]
[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]command[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Executes a server command. Use [ICODE]{player}[/ICODE] as a placeholder for the player name.
[CODE=YAML]
- type: command
  command: "give {player} diamond 1"
  as-console: true     # true = run from console, false = run as player
[/CODE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]item[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Gives an item stack with optional display name, lore, and enchantments.
[CODE=YAML]
- type: item
  material: DIAMOND_SWORD
  amount: 1
  name: "<gradient:#FFD700:#FFA500>Vote Blade</gradient>"
  lore:
    - "<gray>Rewarded for voting"
  enchantments:
    sharpness: 3
    unbreaking: 2
[/CODE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]xp[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Grants vanilla experience points (not levels).
[CODE=YAML]
- type: xp
  amount: 100
[/CODE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]currency[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Deposits money through JExEconomy or Vault.
[CODE=YAML]
- type: currency
  currency: "coins"
  amount: 500
[/CODE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]permission[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Grants a permission node via LuckPerms. Supports timed and server-specific permissions.
[CODE=YAML]
- type: permission
  permission: "essentials.fly"
  duration: "7d"       # Optional — omit for permanent
  server: "survival"   # Optional — omit for global
[/CODE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]sound[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Plays a sound effect at the player's location.
[CODE=YAML]
- type: sound
  sound: ENTITY_PLAYER_LEVELUP
  volume: 1.0
  pitch: 1.2
[/CODE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]particle[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Spawns particles at the player's location.
[CODE=YAML]
- type: particle
  particle: VILLAGER_HAPPY
  count: 30
  offset-x: 0.5
  offset-y: 1.0
  offset-z: 0.5
[/CODE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]title[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Displays a title and subtitle on screen. Durations in ticks (20 ticks = 1 second).
[CODE=YAML]
- type: title
  title: "<green>Thank you!"
  subtitle: "<gray>Your vote has been counted."
  fade-in: 10
  stay: 40
  fade-out: 10
[/CODE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]teleport[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Teleports the player to specific coordinates.
[CODE=YAML]
- type: teleport
  world: "world"
  x: 0.5
  y: 65.0
  z: 0.5
  yaw: 0.0
  pitch: 0.0
[/CODE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]composite[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Bundles multiple rewards into one. All nested rewards are granted together.
[CODE=YAML]
- type: composite
  rewards:
    - type: command
      command: "give {player} emerald 3"
      as-console: true
    - type: sound
      sound: ENTITY_PLAYER_LEVELUP
      volume: 1.0
      pitch: 1.0
[/CODE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]choice[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Opens a selection GUI where the player picks one reward from a set of options.
[CODE=YAML]
- type: choice
  options:
    - type: item
      material: DIAMOND
      amount: 5
    - type: xp
      amount: 500
    - type: currency
      currency: "coins"
      amount: 1000
[/CODE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]custom[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Executes a custom reward handler registered by another plugin via the JExVote API.
[CODE=YAML]
- type: custom
  handler: "my_plugin:special_reward"
  data:
    key: "value"
[/CODE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]chance[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Grants a nested reward with a set probability. Optionally show the chance in menus and announce wins.
[CODE=YAML]
- type: chance
  chance: 0.05         # 5% probability
  show-chance: true
  announce: true
  reward:
    type: command
    command: "give {player} diamond_block 1"
    as-console: true
[/CODE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#9b59b6]lucky[/COLOR][/SIZE]
Rolls one reward from a weighted pool (jackpot). Odds and drop history visible in the rewards menu.
[CODE=YAML]
- type: lucky
  entries:
    - id: "common-coins"
      weight: 50
      reward:
        type: currency
        currency: coins
        amount: 100
    - id: "rare-key"
      weight: 5
      reward:
        type: command
        command: "crate give {player} vote_key 1"
        as-console: true
[/CODE]
[/SPOILER]


